This paper presents a scattering theory for a cubic heterogeneous Schrödinger equation in three dimensions with an inverse square potential.  The equation is given by
\begin{equation*}
\left\{
\begin{array}{cc}
\left\{ -\Delta u + \frac{\gamma}{|x|}u = \lambda |x|^{-\frac{2}{3}} |u|^2 u, \quad x \in \mathbb{R}^3,
\end{array}\right\}
\end{equation*}
with $\lambda > 0$ and $\gamma > 0$.  The outcome of this research is the proof of the local wellposedness and uniform continuity of this system in the form of a semigroup for all time.  Additionally, we established the existence of this system in the form of a quadruple space for all time by combining the methods of the Radon-Von Neumann theorem and the nonlinear scattering theory. 
We were able to demonstrate the continuous imbedding of this system in the form of a quadruple space for all time.  The results of this research cover the entire space of this system in the form of a quadruple space. 
